# Fix for a real false positive: sid:1000001 (rate-based scan rule) was also
# firing on ordinary browser traffic to the Wazuh dashboard itself (port 443),
# since it counts raw SYN volume from a source with no awareness of which
# port is being hit.
#
# This pass rule must be loaded ABOVE sid:1000001 in the rule file - Suricata
# evaluates rules top-down, so traffic matching this rule is excluded before
# it ever reaches the counter in sid:1000001, removing the false positive
# without weakening detection on any other port (confirmed: RDP/3389
# brute-force detection via sid:1000001 still fires correctly after this fix).

pass tcp any any -> $HOME_NET 443 (msg:"PASS Wazuh dashboard HTTPS traffic - exclude from scan detection"; sid:1000002; rev:1;)
